  <static seed="20">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of <m>1-e^{-x/t}\text{,}</m> where <m>t</m> is a positive constant.</p>
<p><m>f'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\exp\mathopen{}\left(\frac{-x}{t}\right)}{t}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Using the chain rule,</p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
          \frac{d}{dx}\left(1-e^{-x/t}\right)
          \amp = -e^{-x/t}\left(-\frac{1}{t}\right)\\
          \amp = \frac{1}{t}e^{-x/t}.
          \end{aligned}</me></p>
</solution>
